        "id": "prefix",
        "text": "A lightweight, non-renewable Vault batch token. Vault's tokens concept page documents the prefixes hvs., hvb. and hvr. and a minimum of 24 random characters after the prefix, and states that the token structure is opaque. This kind begins hvb..",
        "evidenceClass": "provider-documented",
        "temporality": "current",
        "observedAt": "2026-09-20",
        "citations": [
          {
            "kind": "claim",
            "claimId": "provider-source"
          },
          {
            "kind": "source",
            "sourceId": "developer-hashicorp-com-449e83b314"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tool-length",
        "text": "The two scanner rules examined use a length of 90 to 120 characters for Vault tokens. That is corroboration and not a provider statement, since Vault does not publish the full structure.",
        "evidenceClass": "tool-corroborated",
        "temporality": "current",
        "observedAt": "2026-09-20",
        "citations": [
          {
            "kind": "claim",
            "claimId": "tool-corroboration"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "body-opaque",
        "text": "The body beyond the 24-character minimum is opaque in Vault's documentation, so its alphabet and upper length are not provider-established.",
        "evidenceClass": "provider-documented",
        "temporality": "current",
        "observedAt": "2026-09-20",
        "citations": [
          {
